# Rust build artefacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed. This workspace ships binaries (server, client, bot),
# and reproducible builds of a binary need a pinned dependency graph — doubly so
# for a project whose CI gate is a cross-platform determinism hash.

# Fuzzing (cargo-fuzz, from Task 06 onward).
#
# The CORPUS IS COMMITTED — it is the seed set of real encoded messages, and a
# fuzzer starting from valid framing finds far more than one starting from
# noise. Build output and crash artefacts are not.
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/
/fuzz/Cargo.lock

# Criterion benchmark output
/target/criterion/

# Local server state
/server.toml
/world/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Editors and OS
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# VS Code: keep shared settings, ignore per-developer ones
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json

# Task 02b spike artefacts. `measurements.txt` IS committed — the verdict memo
# cites it as the record of what was measured. The OBJ files are regenerated in
# seconds by `cargo run -p subnode-spike --release -- collision` and one of them
# is nearly a megabyte, so they stay out of history.
/spikes/subnode/out/*.obj
